<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Coles sells note to Davids.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Coles sells note to Davids.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coles Myer Ltd said it sold its convertible note in Composite Buyers Ltd to grocery group Davids Ltd for A$32 million.</p>
<p>The retailer said the sale would conclude no later than November 30 this year and produce a gain of A$12 million over book value.  </p>
<p>&quot;Composite Buyers issued the three-year 8.5 percent A$20 million convertible note on June 7, 1994. The sale concludes Coles Myer's external investments in the wholesaling industry,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>Composite is a subsidiary of Davids' unit QIW Ltd.</p>
<p>The subsidiaries were involved in a series of complex takeover bids two years ago which began the rationalisation of Australia's wholesale grocery sector.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
